From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David J. Vandenburgh" <david@vandenburgh.co>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] buildconf: build with USB 3.0 SuperSpeed support

The descriptors for SuperSpeed are already there behind this switch.
With 0006 the packet size follows the link, so the same build works on
a USB 2.0 port and a USB 3 one.
---
diff --git a/inc/buildconf.h b/inc/buildconf.h
index 8d110b2..edf5b4b 100644
--- a/inc/buildconf.h
+++ b/inc/buildconf.h
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 
 #define CONFIG_USB_FS_SUPPORT 1      // USB 1.1 Full speed
 #define CONFIG_USB_HS_SUPPORT 1      // USB 2.0 High speed
-//#define CONFIG_USB_SS_SUPPORT 1    // USB 3.0 SuperSpeed
+#define CONFIG_USB_SS_SUPPORT 1      // USB 3.0 SuperSpeed
 
 #define CONFIG_READ_FILE_BUFFER_SIZE  (1024*1024) // Must be a 2^x value.
 #define CONFIG_MAX_TX_USB_BUFFER_SIZE (16*512)    // Must be a multiple of 512 and be less than CONFIG_READ_FILE_BUFFER_SIZE
